# Bargain makes Johann's Stopgap cost {2} less, {1}{U}, not less than that (CR 601.2f, 702.166a). Bot1 has one Island and an
# Ornithopter to sacrifice, so bargaining is possible but one mana is short of the bargained price of two (and the unbargained
# four). The positive control is johanns-stopgap-bargained-costs-two-less-so-two-mana-bounces-and-draws.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Ornithopter
Johann's Stopgap
Island x4
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
! Bot1.Hand.Johann's Stopgap.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter; Mana: short)

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield = Island; Ornithopter
